# Background Tab Resilience

## Problem

Browsers aggressively conserve resources for inactive tabs:
- `setTimeout`/`setInterval` throttled to ≥1000ms (Chrome)
- After 5 min, full timer freeze (Page Lifecycle freeze)
- Fetch requests are not throttled, but responses may be delayed

## Solution: `~/shared/lib/visibility`

### Page Visibility API

```typescript
import { isTabVisible, onVisibilityChange, onTabResume } from "~/shared/lib/visibility";

// Check current state
if (isTabVisible()) { /* active tab */ }

// Subscribe to changes
onVisibilityChange((visible) => {
  if (!visible) { /* tab hidden — pause non-critical work */ }
});

// Recovery after >30s in background
onTabResume((hiddenDurationMs) => {
  // Re-fetch data, reconnect WebSocket, sync state
  reloadMessages();
  refreshPresence();
});
```

### Resilient Interval

`setInterval` is throttled in background. Use `createResilientInterval` — fires immediately on return to foreground if overdue:

```typescript
import { createResilientInterval } from "~/shared/lib/visibility";

const stop = createResilientInterval(() => {
  fetchPresence();  // 90s polling
}, 90_000);

// cleanup
stop();
```

## Current Integrations

### Event Loop (`app/app.event-loop.ts`)

- Long-poll fetch works in background (not dependent on timers)
- On `BAD_EVENT_QUEUE_ID` → auto re-registration
- `interruptibleSleep()` — sleep via setTimeout, but can be interrupted by `onTabResume`
- On return from background → immediately resumes polling without waiting for timer
- `onReconnect` callback — for full sync after connection loss

### Presence Polling (`widgets/layout/`)

- Uses `setInterval(90_000)` → recommended to replace with `createResilientInterval`

## Rules for AI Agent

### Do not use

```typescript
// ❌ Throttled in background
setInterval(callback, 5000);
setTimeout(callback, longDelay);
```

### Use instead

```typescript
// ✅ Resilient — catchup on resume
createResilientInterval(callback, intervalMs);

// ✅ For one-time tasks — interruptible sleep
onTabResume(() => refetchData());
```

### Fetch/API calls — OK

Fetch requests are NOT throttled in background. Long-poll works normally.

### Animations in background — skip

```typescript
// CSS animations and requestAnimationFrame pause in background — this is normal.
// DO NOT attempt to work around this.
```

## Page Lifecycle States

```
Active → Hidden → Frozen → Discarded
                    ↓          ↓
                  resume    reload (state lost)
```

| State | Timers | Fetch | Our behavior |
|-------|--------|-------|-------------|
| Active | Normal | Normal | Full operation |
| Hidden | Throttled (1s) | OK | Long-poll continues, timers slowed |
| Frozen | Suspended | Suspended | `onTabResume()` for recovery |
| Discarded | Dead | Dead | Full application reload |
